  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Civil Society Support Program II - FCDO - Civil Society Support Program II-2018-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Civil Society Support Program II - FCDO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Programmet f&#xf6;r civila samh&#xe4;llet II (CSSP II) &#xe4;r ett givargemensamt program som ger finansiellt st&#xf6;d till civila samh&#xe4;llet organisationer i Etiopien. 

Programmet finansieras av Irland, DfiD, Norge och Sverige. Den totala budgeten f&#xf6;r programmet uppg&#xe5;r till MSEK 201. Sveriges bidrag &#xe4;r SEK 30 MSEK, Irlands bidrag &#xe4;r 37.8 MSEK, Norge 26 MSEK och Dfids bidrag uppg&#xe5;r till SEK 107 147 000.

Programmet syftar till att bygga en kritisk massa av organisationer som har kapacitet och kompetens att svara mot de behov och r&#xe4;ttigheter som fattiga kvinnor, m&#xe4;n och barn har. Insatsen ska genomf&#xf6;ras under perioden 2018-2021.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Civil Society Support Program II (CSSP II) is a joint Donor Pooled Funding of Civil Society Organizations. Currently, it is funded by Irish Aid, Dfid, Norway and Sweden. The total budget of the program is 201MSEK, out of which Sweden&#x2019;s contribution is 30 MSEK, Irish aid will contribute 37.8MSEK, Norway will contribute 26 MSEK and Dfid&apos;s contribution is of 107, 147,000 SEK.  

The program aims at building a critical mass of CSOs, which have the capability to respond to development priorities determined by the poor. The program is planned to be implemented during the period 2018-2021.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intended impact of CSSP II is contributing to inclusive and accountable governance, and an improved environment for the promotion and protection of the human rights of all Ethiopians through:

1. Increasing the capacity of CSOs to become active organizations and capable advocates on CSSP2 thematic areas.

2. Enhancing citizen-state engagement on CSSP2 strategic themes</narrative>
  </description>
